    "date": "2026-11-03",
    "note": "Transcribed, not captured: tls-client's Brave_146 (Brave on Chromium 146, captured by tls-client from tls.peet.ws on 2026-03-27) has the ClientHello and HTTP/2 of Chrome 146 byte for byte — JA4_r, JA3N and the Akamai string equal those of the captured chrome-142-macos, checked here by building its spec through tls-client's uTLS fork — so they are replayed from chrome-142-macos, as chrome-146-windows does. tls-client describes no headers. The header set is chrome-146-windows's (wreq-util's Chrome 146 on Windows) with the traits measured on Brave 1.98.63 here (brave-1.98-windows): Sec-GPC: 1 after Accept on every request, no application/signed-exchange in Accept, the Brave brand in Google Chrome's place in sec-ch-ua, and the Accept-Language weight Brave draws per site and session. Brave 1.88 is the release on Chromium 146 (v1.88.138, Chromium 146.0.7680.178). No client hints, like the Chrome 146 it stands beside."
  },
